 "text": "Hey, nice surprise. How are you? Get it into the freezer right after it' cooked. If it' from freezer bags, leave it alone for a couple of uses before you take it out. Ice cubes are much easier to grab. Put the food straight into frozen ice cube trays so they don't sit in water. Get the meat out of its casing before you freeze it, the casing spoils quickly. And move it to a cooler with ice when it's frozen. Put it in a bag inside with a frozen bottle of water. The water will stay frozen for hours, keeping the meat from being open. Yes, change it every few hours. Cold from the freezer takes priority, and the bottle will stay cold longer than you expect.",
